  "description": "Allows an external client to set the state of the \n\t\tsurrogate.  Setting the surrogate state may be used to manually override a state that is\n\t\tpreventing launch or recovery, or to correct an incorrect or unknown state.  This message\n\t\tmay also be used by an external client responsible for assessing the launch / recovery \n\t\tstate for the surrogate in cases where the surrogate itself cannot fully determine that \n\t\tstate.",
